# Wave W17-S (Route 129): lee rock — crater-lee rock standing in the lane\u2019s water: a grey shore rock drawn shadow-side — its body in lee shade, its light standing only along the north-west edges where the crater\u2019s shadow breaks, foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it (design: the crater\u2019s bulk shadowing the north horizon, the lane in its lee). Route 129\u2019s own rock — the fleet\u2019s only shadow-side rock: split from Route 126\u2019s massive-jointed crater rock (its parent register) by the lee finish — the same crater, read from its sheltered side — and from Route 128\u2019s warm-seamed rock by temperature.
